---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Wrexham University"
  category="Education | Upcoming International Mobility"
  year="2026"
  description="Upcoming international academic mobility at Wrexham University in the United Kingdom."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    Upcoming international academic mobility in the United Kingdom |
    expanding my engineering education through a new academic,
    cultural and professional environment.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | Mobility
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Continuing my international engineering journey.
      </h2>

      <p>
        As part of my engineering degree at ICAM Grand Paris Sud,
        I am preparing a new international mobility period
        at Wrexham University in the United Kingdom.
      </p>

      <p>
        This experience will complement my previous academic mobility
        in Poland and further strengthen my ability to study,
        communicate and collaborate in an international environment.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Objectives
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Expanding beyond my technical background.
      </h2>

      <p>
        The mobility is intended to broaden my engineering perspective
        while developing additional skills in an English-speaking
        academic environment.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>International academic experience</li>
        <li>Technical communication in English</li>
        <li>Cross-cultural collaboration</li>
        <li>Engineering adaptability</li>
        <li>Professional autonomy</li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | International Development
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Building an international engineering profile.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Working and studying in different countries is an important
        part of the profile I am building as an engineer.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each international experience exposes me to different
        approaches to education, industry and technical collaboration |
        helping me develop a broader understanding of engineering
        beyond a single national context.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | English Environment
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Engineering through English.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Studying in the United Kingdom will provide an opportunity
        to use English continuously in academic and technical contexts.
      </p>

      <p>
        This will complement my current English level
        and reinforce my ability to communicate engineering concepts
        clearly within international teams.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | Perspective
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Preparing for an international career.
      </h2>

      <p>
        This mobility is part of a broader objective |
        building a career in advanced engineering, robotics
        and research within international organisations.
      </p>

      <p>
        Experiences in France, Switzerland, Poland
        and the United Kingdom progressively strengthen
        this international dimension of my engineering profile.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      06 | Status
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Upcoming mobility.
      </h2>

      <p>
        This section will be updated as the mobility progresses |
        including coursework, projects, technical activities
        and key outcomes from the experience.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>